{"title":"Edge","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>An <b>edge</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">polygon</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polyhedron\" title=\"Polyhedron\">polyhedron</a> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line_segment\" title=\"Line segment\">line segment</a> whose endpoints are two adjacent <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\">vertices</a> of the figure.  In the case of polygons, an edge joins two consecutive vertices.  In the case of polyhedra, an edge joins two vertices and is the boundary between two adjacent <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Face\" title=\"Face\">faces</a>. An edge can also be part of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Graph_(graph_theory)\" title=\"Graph (graph theory)\">graph</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonal\" title=\"Diagonal\">Diagonal</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Edge&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018083300\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 15/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 253/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,ca